1
00:00:02,690 --> 00:00:04,040
You're an idiot.

2
00:00:04,480 --> 00:00:07,380
It's bad enough you believed her, but then you gave up?

3
00:00:07,810 --> 00:00:09,560
Please, forgive me Colonel.

4
00:00:09,880 --> 00:00:11,110
You've gotta stay strong.

5
00:00:11,380 --> 00:00:13,560
And don't you ever give up on living.

6
00:00:13,930 --> 00:00:17,000
I need to know you can keep
your cool no matter what happens.

7
00:00:18,070 --> 00:00:18,880
Sir.

8
00:00:20,110 --> 00:00:22,810
I'm gonna continue to
rely on you to watch my back.

9
00:00:23,020 --> 00:00:24,100
Don't let me down.

10
00:00:24,340 --> 00:00:27,200
You oughta think about taking
your own advice, Colonel.

11
00:00:27,430 --> 00:00:29,760
Since you were the one
who abandoned his post.

12
00:00:29,780 --> 00:00:31,750
Hey! Shut up, Havoc—ow!

13
00:00:31,750 --> 00:00:33,000
[GROANS]

14
00:00:33,670 --> 00:00:34,780
And what the hell?

15
00:00:34,990 --> 00:00:36,840
Why are we even in the same room?

16
00:00:37,080 --> 00:00:39,040
At my rank I should have my own room.

17
00:00:39,100 --> 00:00:40,060
With hot nurse...

18
00:00:40,400 --> 00:00:41,780
Try to understand, sir.

19
00:00:42,310 --> 00:00:44,820
It's easier to guard the
two of you in the same place.

20
00:00:44,890 --> 00:00:46,260
Which reminds me...

21
00:00:46,930 --> 00:00:49,520
Why haven't they tried to kill us yet?

22
00:00:50,100 --> 00:00:51,660
What's wrong with you?!

23
00:00:51,760 --> 00:00:54,640
How could you let that bastard go
after what he did?

24
00:00:54,680 --> 00:00:57,060
You should've yanked his spine
out of his mouth!

25
00:00:57,840 --> 00:01:00,560
Lust... He killed Lust...

26
00:01:00,680 --> 00:01:03,860
It's not too late to kill him,
so get to it!

27
00:01:03,970 --> 00:01:05,660
We can use Mustang.

28
00:01:06,100 --> 00:01:08,240
He's worthless if we kill him, however.

29
00:01:08,500 --> 00:01:09,580
Use him?

30
00:01:09,880 --> 00:01:10,600
Hold on...

31
00:01:10,660 --> 00:01:12,060
You mean the portal?

32
00:01:12,260 --> 00:01:14,800
[CHUCKLES]
You don't need to worry about it

33
00:01:14,890 --> 00:01:16,240
And forget Mustang.

34
00:01:16,420 --> 00:01:18,860
Father wants me to handle him.

35
00:01:21,840 --> 00:01:27,560
Masshiro na keshiki ni ima sasowarete

36
00:01:27,560 --> 00:01:32,980
Boku wa yuku yo mada minu sekai e

37
00:01:39,540 --> 00:01:42,860
Maigo no mama tabi shiteita

38
00:01:42,860 --> 00:01:45,540
nezumiiro no sora no shita

39
00:01:45,540 --> 00:01:51,840
Higawari no chizu
ikutsumo no yume ga nijinde ita

40
00:01:51,840 --> 00:01:57,960
Itsuka wa sa chippoke na
boku no kono hohaba demo

41
00:01:57,960 --> 00:02:04,040
Ano kumo no mukou made yukeru kana

42
00:02:04,180 --> 00:02:10,200
Tsuyogatte kizutsuita kokoro sukashita you ni

43
00:02:10,340 --> 00:02:17,080
Furidashita amatsubutachi ga
ranhansha kurikaesu

44
00:02:17,260 --> 00:02:22,620
Massugu na hikari ga kousa shite

45
00:02:22,840 --> 00:02:29,340
Yukusaki mo tsugenu mama
dokomademo tsukinukeru

46
00:02:29,340 --> 00:02:35,100
Awai zanzou ryoume ni yakistukete

47
00:02:35,100 --> 00:02:41,300
Kono sora no shita donna toko ni ite mo

48
00:02:41,300 --> 00:02:48,120
Todoku hazu nanda mada minu sekai e

49
00:02:52,330 --> 00:02:54,260
What if I've started to rot?

50
00:02:54,260 --> 00:02:55,240
BOTH: Huh?

51
00:02:55,640 --> 00:02:59,600
I doubt that my body's getting any nutrients...
or any sleep, either!

52
00:02:59,860 --> 00:03:02,600
So even if we get it
back from over there...

53
00:03:02,660 --> 00:03:05,560
[DISTORTED] Brother... Winry...

54
00:03:05,560 --> 00:03:07,410
[SHRIEKS]

55
00:03:08,500 --> 00:03:10,000
Is he right, Ed?

56
00:03:10,760 --> 00:03:11,620
[SIGH]

57
00:03:11,740 --> 00:03:13,580
Now this is just a hypothesis...

58
00:03:13,720 --> 00:03:17,500
But I was thinking about the transmutation
and trying to retrace our process.

59
00:03:17,660 --> 00:03:21,580
You remember how we mixed our blood
to create a blueprint for mom's soul?

60
00:03:21,700 --> 00:03:22,660
Yeah.

61
00:03:22,740 --> 00:03:25,600
Well, right after that
we passed through the portal,

62
00:03:25,760 --> 00:03:27,560
where we were both deconstructed.

63
00:03:29,440 --> 00:03:30,580
It's a slim chance...

64
00:03:30,740 --> 00:03:34,820
But I think it's possible our spirits
might've gotten tangled up in the process.

65
00:03:35,800 --> 00:03:37,280
What are you saying?

66
00:03:37,330 --> 00:03:40,440
I'm trying to explain that our
bodies might be connected somehow,

67
00:03:40,460 --> 00:03:43,120
even though I'm
here and your body's over there.

68
00:03:43,260 --> 00:03:44,100
See...

69
00:03:44,110 --> 00:03:47,180
That might actually explain why I'm so sh...

70
00:03:48,560 --> 00:03:50,020
Sh...

71
00:03:50,860 --> 00:03:52,080
Short.

72
00:03:52,150 --> 00:03:55,280
- He admitted it.
- He's starting to face reality!

73
00:03:55,420 --> 00:03:56,240
So...

74
00:03:56,640 --> 00:04:00,340
You think you've been supplying
all the nutrients for Al's body, too?

75
00:04:00,740 --> 00:04:02,630
That seems a little far-fetched.

76
00:04:02,860 --> 00:04:04,820
Well what's your explanation?

77
00:04:05,020 --> 00:04:07,480
You don't grow because
you refuse to drink your milk.

78
00:04:07,640 --> 00:04:10,380
- Don't start with that again!
- Well, it's true!

79
00:04:10,400 --> 00:04:13,080
It seems like brother is always sleeping...

80
00:04:13,100 --> 00:04:16,400
I wonder if his body could
be resting for mine as well?

81
00:04:16,420 --> 00:04:18,360
...you start drinking it, you have to!

82
00:04:18,360 --> 00:04:19,460
- It's not gonna happen!
- Drink it!

83
00:04:19,460 --> 00:04:20,050
No!

84
00:04:20,050 --> 00:04:21,100
- Fine, stay a runt!
- [AL LAUGHING]

85
00:04:21,120 --> 00:04:22,060
I'm not a runt!

86
00:04:22,140 --> 00:04:23,160
I hope so, at least.

87
00:04:23,160 --> 00:04:25,960
- ...Never!
- I'll make you!
- Just try!

88
00:04:28,220 --> 00:04:29,880
Are you here to visit the Colonel?

89
00:04:29,900 --> 00:04:32,040
Mr. Havoc is recovering too.

90
00:04:32,290 --> 00:04:34,370
We figured we should pay our respects.

91
00:04:34,540 --> 00:04:36,340
I definitely owe it to the Colonel.

92
00:04:36,360 --> 00:04:38,440
He saved me right the last second.

93
00:04:40,060 --> 00:04:42,280
Are you also dropping by for a visit?

94
00:04:42,880 --> 00:04:44,560
And bringing a little present.

95
00:04:46,520 --> 00:04:50,720
I counted the number of steps it took to get
to the basement under the Third Laboratory.

96
00:04:50,900 --> 00:04:54,180
And I was able to calculate
the approximate location of that doorway.

97
00:04:55,260 --> 00:04:57,400
It's not exact, since the hallway curved

98
00:04:57,670 --> 00:05:01,370
But I was able to deduce a radius
with the lab at the center.

99
00:05:03,280 --> 00:05:04,920
That's Central Command?!

100
00:05:05,020 --> 00:05:07,120
But this is even more alarming...

101
00:05:07,500 --> 00:05:09,260
It's the Presidential Estate.

102
00:05:09,520 --> 00:05:11,960
Right above where we found
the homunculi.

103
00:05:12,460 --> 00:05:17,150
Which means there's a very real possibility
the Fuhrer is connected to them.

104
00:05:18,580 --> 00:05:19,930
But that doesn't make sense.

105
00:05:20,340 --> 00:05:23,940
Why did he kill Greed and his group
if he's connected to them?

106
00:05:24,220 --> 00:05:25,920
Strange he killed them anyway...

107
00:05:26,140 --> 00:05:29,020
Why would he slaughter them
before interrogating them?

108
00:05:29,820 --> 00:05:31,080
Strange, all right.

109
00:05:31,240 --> 00:05:32,960
Damn inscrutable.

110
00:05:34,740 --> 00:05:38,540
One thing's for sure, the enemy's infiltrated
high up the command.

111
00:05:38,620 --> 00:05:41,350
So extreme caution is
necessary at all times

112
00:05:41,660 --> 00:05:42,780
And Fullmetal?

113
00:05:43,060 --> 00:05:45,160
- Watch yourself.
- [GASP]

114
00:05:48,460 --> 00:05:51,260
The Fuhrer...working with the Homunculi...

115
00:05:53,620 --> 00:05:56,120
This could be bigger
than I ever dreamed.

116
00:05:56,400 --> 00:05:58,680
I'm starting to worry that it's too big.

117
00:05:59,020 --> 00:06:00,640
All the more reason to pursue it.

118
00:06:01,480 --> 00:06:01,900
So.

119
00:06:02,320 --> 00:06:04,340
I hope you're ready
to work yourselves ragged.

120
00:06:04,360 --> 00:06:06,530
Oh, yeah. About that, Colonel?

121
00:06:07,180 --> 00:06:09,040
I think you're gonna have to count me out.

122
00:06:11,900 --> 00:06:13,540
Your work requires legs

123
00:06:14,160 --> 00:06:16,160
- And I can't feel mine.
- [GASPS]

124
00:06:18,000 --> 00:06:19,880
I hate to say it,

125
00:06:19,960 --> 00:06:21,290
but I'm retired.

126
00:06:28,100 --> 00:06:29,270
Hello.

127
00:06:29,760 --> 00:06:30,720
Hey.

128
00:06:31,060 --> 00:06:32,460
What brings you down here?

129
00:06:32,720 --> 00:06:34,190
Back problems.

130
00:06:34,330 --> 00:06:38,150
My spine can't stand all the standing
that comes with being coroner.

131
00:06:41,200 --> 00:06:45,440
I got a sinking feeling when I heard
you were the person that scorched that Thing.

132
00:06:45,840 --> 00:06:47,690
Are you plotting something?

133
00:06:47,840 --> 00:06:51,640
You suspect a plot, but you still ID'd the "thing" as Maria Ross.

134
00:06:52,000 --> 00:06:54,060
Three cheers for old war buddies, huh?

135
00:06:54,220 --> 00:06:55,870
Old war buddies, my butt.

136
00:06:56,200 --> 00:06:57,680
More like accomplices.

137
00:06:58,360 --> 00:07:00,970
You'd incinerate 'em
and I'd dissect what's left.

138
00:07:01,450 --> 00:07:04,670
We treated them like rats
and Ishval was the lab.

139
00:07:09,220 --> 00:07:11,040
I know you like to play with fire,

140
00:07:11,040 --> 00:07:13,620
but someone'll get burnt
if you push this too far.

141
00:07:14,060 --> 00:07:15,700
You should have warned me earlier.

142
00:07:15,840 --> 00:07:16,380
Huh?

143
00:07:18,820 --> 00:07:20,690
Did somebody get injured?

144
00:07:22,140 --> 00:07:23,640
One of my men.

145
00:07:25,420 --> 00:07:26,740
He was paralyzed.

146
00:07:27,320 --> 00:07:28,700
From the waist down.

147
00:07:34,540 --> 00:07:35,480
Damn.

148
00:07:35,640 --> 00:07:39,260
They only let me smoke one of these a day,
and I go and waste it.

149
00:07:40,540 --> 00:07:41,540
Jeez.

150
00:07:41,590 --> 00:07:45,080
You know I thought I'd retire because
of a woman, but not like this.

151
00:07:46,120 --> 00:07:47,600
So what happens next?

152
00:07:49,180 --> 00:07:51,440
My family owns a grocery store.

153
00:07:52,420 --> 00:07:54,180
And I can at least take calls.

154
00:07:54,980 --> 00:07:56,980
Isn't automail an option?

155
00:07:59,220 --> 00:08:02,060
The nerves in my lower spine
are completely severed,

156
00:08:02,080 --> 00:08:04,430
and they can't make those out of steel.

157
00:08:04,640 --> 00:08:05,400
Tch.

158
00:08:06,000 --> 00:08:08,240
The retired life
doesn't suit you.

159
00:08:13,080 --> 00:08:13,940
Colonel.

160
00:08:13,940 --> 00:08:14,660
Hmm?

161
00:08:15,360 --> 00:08:16,920
There's still hope for Havoc.

162
00:08:17,380 --> 00:08:18,920
Fullmetal passed this onto me.

163
00:08:21,460 --> 00:08:22,910
Dr. Marcoh, huh?

164
00:08:23,660 --> 00:08:26,200
Medical alchemist in possession of a...

165
00:08:26,260 --> 00:08:28,220
Philosopher's stone?!

166
00:08:28,420 --> 00:08:30,420
Well, sir, should I find him?

167
00:08:31,750 --> 00:08:32,920
Permission granted.

168
00:08:33,040 --> 00:08:34,390
Get going.

169
00:08:38,900 --> 00:08:40,320
Oh, Major!

170
00:08:40,740 --> 00:08:41,340
Hmm?

171
00:08:41,380 --> 00:08:43,030
I didn't expect
you back so soon.

172
00:08:43,500 --> 00:08:45,620
How did you enjoy
your vacation to the east?

173
00:08:45,620 --> 00:08:47,620
[GRUNTING]

174
00:08:47,620 --> 00:08:48,250
Shh!

175
00:08:48,250 --> 00:08:50,480
Loose lips sink ships, Major.

176
00:08:51,040 --> 00:08:54,260
The scenery was luminous
and the women desirable.

177
00:08:54,300 --> 00:08:55,100
Ha...

178
00:08:55,540 --> 00:08:57,280
Uh, oh! Uh, before I forget,

179
00:08:57,400 --> 00:09:00,080
this just arrived from the Provost Marshal's office.

180
00:09:00,720 --> 00:09:03,540
It's an urgent bulletin
for all State Alchemists.

181
00:09:04,560 --> 00:09:06,020
Good heavens!

182
00:09:09,580 --> 00:09:10,700
How'd it go?

183
00:09:10,800 --> 00:09:11,420
Easy.

184
00:09:11,560 --> 00:09:15,670
I told them I was a State Alchemist and they
let me right in with no questions asked.

185
00:09:16,020 --> 00:09:17,690
Did you find the basement?

186
00:09:17,800 --> 00:09:18,760
There wasn't one.

187
00:09:18,760 --> 00:09:19,720
[GASP]

188
00:09:20,350 --> 00:09:23,450
But it did find a trace
of some hasty alchemy.

189
00:09:24,200 --> 00:09:27,890
It was stupid of us to think that
they wouldn't seal up the entrance.

190
00:09:29,020 --> 00:09:29,740
I guess so.

191
00:09:30,060 --> 00:09:33,400
Where else are we gonna to find a
homunculus if we can get down there?

192
00:09:34,870 --> 00:09:35,930
I'm not sure.

193
00:09:36,680 --> 00:09:40,060
Remember how they told me I was their sacrifice,
and they needed me alive?

194
00:09:40,140 --> 00:09:41,580
They told me the same thing.

195
00:09:41,860 --> 00:09:44,990
Lust told me that when
she found out I opened the portal.

196
00:09:45,060 --> 00:09:46,750
Well there's one piece of the puzzle.

197
00:09:46,940 --> 00:09:48,400
They're looking for alchemists...

198
00:09:48,400 --> 00:09:51,710
that managed to open the portal
and make it back out alive.

199
00:09:51,940 --> 00:09:54,860
But the real question is
why they wanna sacrifice us.

200
00:09:55,140 --> 00:09:57,700
So, we'll have to beat an answer out of them.

201
00:09:58,360 --> 00:10:00,000
- Edward, wait!
- What the...

202
00:10:00,220 --> 00:10:01,600
Is that Sergeant Brosh?

203
00:10:01,600 --> 00:10:02,860
I'm glad I found you.

204
00:10:03,020 --> 00:10:04,760
Yeah, why don't you tell me what's wrong?

205
00:10:04,760 --> 00:10:07,000
You should go back to your hotel right now.

206
00:10:07,440 --> 00:10:09,360
I can escort you if you want me to.

207
00:10:11,260 --> 00:10:13,360
Attention all military personnel,

208
00:10:13,610 --> 00:10:16,740
It has been verified that
Scar has returned to central.

209
00:10:16,860 --> 00:10:18,720
Three casualties have been reported.

210
00:10:19,100 --> 00:10:21,540
All confirmed as State Alchemists.

211
00:10:22,220 --> 00:10:23,840
According to eyewitness reports,

212
00:10:23,940 --> 00:10:28,040
he is described as an Ishvalan,
with an X-shaped scar on his forehead.

213
00:10:28,280 --> 00:10:31,920
Other identifiable markings include
a tattoo on his right arm.

214
00:10:34,320 --> 00:10:35,560
A tattoo.

215
00:10:36,440 --> 00:10:37,890
It was him.

216
00:10:38,640 --> 00:10:40,470
Fullmetal Alchemist

217
00:10:42,120 --> 00:10:43,740
Fullmetal Alchemist.

218
00:10:44,960 --> 00:10:48,130
So you're saying that
Scar killed Winry's parents?

219
00:10:48,360 --> 00:10:50,820
I don't know for certain,
but that's the way it looks.

220
00:10:51,160 --> 00:10:52,470
Poor Winry...

221
00:10:52,760 --> 00:10:53,520
Brother,

222
00:10:53,540 --> 00:10:55,560
you weren't planning on
telling her, were you?

223
00:10:55,700 --> 00:10:56,780
Of course not, Al.

224
00:10:57,540 --> 00:11:00,320
I couldn't stand to be the one
to make her cry again.

225
00:11:01,420 --> 00:11:02,800
Neither could i.

226
00:11:04,490 --> 00:11:07,430
It's the last thing I wanna do,
but we have to confront Scar

227
00:11:07,790 --> 00:11:09,080
To find out if he did it?

228
00:11:09,520 --> 00:11:11,030
Well, that's one reason.

229
00:11:11,240 --> 00:11:12,900
But there is another.

230
00:11:13,060 --> 00:11:15,100
We're gonna lure out the Homunculi.

231
00:11:15,520 --> 00:11:16,280
[GASP]

232
00:11:16,280 --> 00:11:19,100
They need us alive
for their sacrifice, don't they?

233
00:11:19,400 --> 00:11:23,030
So I doubt they'll be willing to just
stand by while Scar kills us.

234
00:11:23,750 --> 00:11:24,590
You think so?

235
00:11:25,100 --> 00:11:27,320
Sounds like a pretty
big gamble to me.

236
00:11:27,710 --> 00:11:29,570
Well it's much better
than doin' nothing.

237
00:11:29,990 --> 00:11:30,680
Oh, really?

238
00:11:30,860 --> 00:11:33,420
Because Scar literally torn us apart
the last time.

239
00:11:34,610 --> 00:11:36,880
Well, we've...gotten stronger...

240
00:11:36,880 --> 00:11:38,540
in these past few months...

241
00:11:39,060 --> 00:11:41,390
What happens if the Homunculi do show up?

242
00:11:41,640 --> 00:11:43,120
How are you gonna catch one?!

243
00:11:43,190 --> 00:11:46,400
They're super strong,
and they pretty much can't die!

244
00:11:46,520 --> 00:11:48,960
Can't die? Was that hyperbole?

245
00:11:49,080 --> 00:11:50,900
Or are they actually immortal?

246
00:11:52,500 --> 00:11:54,400
Why don't we lock the windows?

247
00:11:55,820 --> 00:11:58,560
Count us in,
we'd love to help you guys.

248
00:11:58,560 --> 00:11:59,420
Why's that?

249
00:11:59,540 --> 00:12:02,080
I can't say I care about the military stuff,

250
00:12:02,080 --> 00:12:05,500
but it sounds like these Homunculi are
just what we've been looking for.

251
00:12:07,860 --> 00:12:08,720
What's wrong?

252
00:12:08,780 --> 00:12:10,440
You look kindaskeptical.

253
00:12:10,840 --> 00:12:14,180
Don't get me wrong, I am grateful for
the help you've already given...

254
00:12:14,180 --> 00:12:16,800
- But this...
- You've got better odds with more help.

255
00:12:18,080 --> 00:12:19,490
I'm serious about this.

256
00:12:19,960 --> 00:12:22,530
This could be what
rescues my clan.

257
00:12:28,240 --> 00:12:29,740
Alright then.

258
00:12:30,350 --> 00:12:32,800
Just remember, we're in this together.

259
00:12:33,080 --> 00:12:34,980
I promise not to
run off with them.

260
00:12:35,460 --> 00:12:37,040
I owe you that much.

261
00:12:37,300 --> 00:12:38,320
What for?

262
00:12:40,500 --> 00:12:41,820
[CASH REGISTER DING]

263
00:12:41,900 --> 00:12:44,140
- Is...this...for room service?!

264
00:12:44,140 --> 00:12:45,640
Uhh... [NERVOUS LAUGH]

265
00:12:46,080 --> 00:12:48,020
You're damn right you owe me!

266
00:12:48,020 --> 00:12:49,260
[WINDOW SMASHES]
BOTH: Woo!

267
00:12:49,300 --> 00:12:50,980
Will you guys shut up?!

268
00:12:50,980 --> 00:12:53,320
Do you know how early
I have to wake up tomorrow?!

269
00:12:53,420 --> 00:12:55,140
Oh right, I forgot!

270
00:12:55,180 --> 00:12:57,520
You're catching an early train to Rush Va—

271
00:12:57,520 --> 00:13:00,180
[GASP]
[METAL SMASHING]

272
00:13:00,280 --> 00:13:02,300
Y'know what? You should cancel that.

273
00:13:02,440 --> 00:13:04,180
Why don't you stick around and relax?

274
00:13:04,200 --> 00:13:05,000
Huh?

275
00:13:05,440 --> 00:13:07,660
I mean it's just that...y'know, well...

276
00:13:07,740 --> 00:13:08,460
There's...

277
00:13:08,520 --> 00:13:10,960
Always a chance my arm could get broken.

278
00:13:11,340 --> 00:13:12,110
Or even...

279
00:13:12,180 --> 00:13:12,920
destroyed...

280
00:13:12,940 --> 00:13:15,380
[CRASH]
Are you planning on destroying it?!

281
00:13:15,560 --> 00:13:18,380
ED: [WHIMPERING]
AL: I've got your soul, brother!

282
00:13:19,280 --> 00:13:20,580
I can't believe you.

283
00:13:21,500 --> 00:13:24,360
Just promise you won't
do anything too dangerous.

284
00:13:25,230 --> 00:13:26,230
BOTH: Uh...

285
00:13:28,960 --> 00:13:32,180
[BIRDS CHIRPING]

286
00:13:32,300 --> 00:13:33,260
[KNOCKING]
Hey, Doc.

287
00:13:33,440 --> 00:13:34,640
Are you home?

288
00:13:34,920 --> 00:13:36,700
I could use your help with something.

289
00:13:38,810 --> 00:13:39,810
Huh?

290
00:13:45,460 --> 00:13:46,520
Damn.

291
00:13:49,700 --> 00:13:51,150
Is that so?

292
00:13:51,280 --> 00:13:53,220
Report back to base.

293
00:13:54,800 --> 00:13:56,580
Yet another dead end.

294
00:13:58,860 --> 00:14:01,260
[DOOR OPENS]

295
00:14:03,350 --> 00:14:06,060
Well, if you'll excuse me.

296
00:14:10,550 --> 00:14:11,270
Who was that?

297
00:14:11,720 --> 00:14:14,820
My mother, and an officer
from the veterans council.

298
00:14:16,000 --> 00:14:18,380
I've decided to go
ahead with my retirement.

299
00:14:19,600 --> 00:14:22,590
I don't know for certain if
your wounds are inoperable.

300
00:14:22,920 --> 00:14:25,220
I'm not dumb enough
to think i have a chance.

301
00:14:25,670 --> 00:14:26,790
I'm useless.

302
00:14:27,320 --> 00:14:28,380
You're wrong.

303
00:14:29,120 --> 00:14:32,240
Look, don't try and tell me
you need upon that can't move.

304
00:14:36,140 --> 00:14:38,400
And don't you
look at me like that.

305
00:14:39,110 --> 00:14:40,310
Forget about me.

306
00:14:40,790 --> 00:14:42,360
Move on already.

307
00:14:42,420 --> 00:14:44,480
You don't have time
to worry about me!

308
00:14:44,760 --> 00:14:47,480
You need to think about the promise
you made General Hughes,

309
00:14:47,520 --> 00:14:49,250
- instead of pitying me!
- Lieutenant Havoc!

310
00:14:55,720 --> 00:14:57,820
Just let me get on with my life.

311
00:14:59,600 --> 00:15:00,940
I beg you.

312
00:15:07,840 --> 00:15:09,150
- All right.
- [GASP]

313
00:15:09,440 --> 00:15:10,620
You're cut loose.

314
00:15:16,000 --> 00:15:18,440
I'll leave you behind
so you can catch up.

315
00:15:19,720 --> 00:15:21,020
I've got to keep moving,

316
00:15:21,290 --> 00:15:23,400
but I'll see you at the top.

317
00:15:25,820 --> 00:15:27,080
[DOOR OPENS AND CLOSES]

318
00:15:27,560 --> 00:15:28,980
He doesn't give up.

319
00:15:29,360 --> 00:15:31,960
He didn't even think about
turning his back on me.

320
00:15:31,960 --> 00:15:33,780
And I had given up on living.

321
00:15:34,300 --> 00:15:36,380
It's not in him to
abandon others.

322
00:15:36,640 --> 00:15:37,720
He refuses to.

323
00:15:40,010 --> 00:15:41,430
He's a fool.

324
00:15:41,540 --> 00:15:43,220
He's not gonna make it to the top.

325
00:15:43,520 --> 00:15:47,150
This country will chew him up
if he keeps on acting this soft.

326
00:15:48,100 --> 00:15:49,540
Well I don't know about that.

327
00:15:49,720 --> 00:15:52,280
This country needs
a fool like that man.

328
00:15:58,720 --> 00:16:01,000
I need you to bring me my uniform.

329
00:16:01,240 --> 00:16:03,720
But you're not ready to leave the hospital yet, Colonel.

330
00:16:03,760 --> 00:16:05,340
Just go get it.

331
00:16:10,500 --> 00:16:11,880
Right away, sir.

332
00:16:14,510 --> 00:16:17,620
Oh that's my livelihood, you idiot!

333
00:16:17,720 --> 00:16:19,640
U-Uh, I'm really sorry sir.

334
00:16:19,960 --> 00:16:23,040
Ah, well sorry's not gonna fix my stand.

335
00:16:23,480 --> 00:16:25,600
Looks like you could use some help!

336
00:16:25,600 --> 00:16:26,160
BOTH: Huh?

337
00:16:26,720 --> 00:16:28,580
It's a good thing I happened by!

338
00:16:28,580 --> 00:16:31,280
Edward Elric: State Alchemist at large!

339
00:16:35,020 --> 00:16:36,620
Wow, that's amazing!

340
00:16:36,820 --> 00:16:38,280
Thank you very much, sir!

341
00:16:38,280 --> 00:16:40,500
Please, you have to let me pay you for this.

342
00:16:40,760 --> 00:16:41,760
Pay me?

343
00:16:41,810 --> 00:16:44,060
Thats not necessary,
but thank you!

344
00:16:44,270 --> 00:16:46,980
Could you please help me
with my broken vase?

345
00:16:47,020 --> 00:16:49,080
It's a priceless family heirloom.

346
00:16:49,080 --> 00:16:51,080
Why no problem at all! [CLAP]

347
00:16:52,060 --> 00:16:53,360
[CROWD OOH'S]

348
00:16:54,220 --> 00:16:55,320
[CROWD OOH'S]

349
00:16:56,600 --> 00:16:58,100
[CROWD AHH'S]

350
00:17:00,860 --> 00:17:05,060
That's right, I'm here to help!
I'm your friendly neighborhood State Alchemist.

351
00:17:05,300 --> 00:17:07,780
Don't forget: I'm Edward Elric!

352
00:17:07,780 --> 00:17:09,780
[CROWD CHEERING]

353
00:17:10,520 --> 00:17:11,780
[SNEEZE]

354
00:17:12,680 --> 00:17:17,250
[CHUCKLING] I'm pretty sure everyone in
Central knows my name by now.

355
00:17:17,330 --> 00:17:19,360
Well you were a little over the top.

356
00:17:21,530 --> 00:17:24,860
When did you become so theatrical, Fullmetal?

357
00:17:25,120 --> 00:17:25,980
Colonel?

358
00:17:26,420 --> 00:17:28,440
Shouldn't you still
be in the hospital?

359
00:17:28,580 --> 00:17:29,580
Probably.

360
00:17:31,040 --> 00:17:32,810
I heard about Lieutenant Havoc.

361
00:17:33,290 --> 00:17:35,660
- I'm sure Doctor Marcoh—
- Hold on.

362
00:17:36,350 --> 00:17:37,940
People are watching us.

363
00:17:38,180 --> 00:17:39,360
Get in.

364
00:17:41,180 --> 00:17:43,380
On second thought let's get out.

365
00:17:45,020 --> 00:17:46,370
Dr. Marcoh's gone missing?

366
00:17:46,910 --> 00:17:47,660
Looks like it.

367
00:17:47,900 --> 00:17:49,920
They probably took him captive.

368
00:17:51,320 --> 00:17:53,150
There's something else
we need to talk about.

369
00:17:53,570 --> 00:17:55,460
I'm sure you've heard that Scar's back.

370
00:17:55,970 --> 00:17:59,610
So what's with the showboating,
do you want him to find you?

371
00:18:00,740 --> 00:18:02,480
Yeah that's exactly what I want.

372
00:18:03,110 --> 00:18:05,340
I need to fight him,
and you can't talk me out of it.

373
00:18:05,340 --> 00:18:07,100
Have you lost your mind?!

374
00:18:07,100 --> 00:18:10,410
Did you forget the way he
tore you apart in East City?

375
00:18:10,420 --> 00:18:13,600
Oooh, sounds like the Colonel's scared of big, bad Scar.

376
00:18:13,620 --> 00:18:17,560
I'm not surprised considering how useless
you were against him! [LAUGHING]

377
00:18:17,780 --> 00:18:20,200
That wasn't my fault,
it was raining that day!

378
00:18:20,220 --> 00:18:23,460
Was it raining when you got
beat up and sent to the hospital?

379
00:18:23,500 --> 00:18:25,600
You're still useless!

380
00:18:25,600 --> 00:18:26,920
Shut you mouth, Fullmetal!

381
00:18:30,200 --> 00:18:31,520
Guess he got your invite.

382
00:18:31,790 --> 00:18:32,600
You okay?

383
00:18:32,810 --> 00:18:35,910
He'd think it was raining
the way your forehead's dripping.

384
00:18:36,220 --> 00:18:37,070
Hold it!

385
00:18:37,460 --> 00:18:38,450
Don't shoot, Lieutenant.

386
00:18:38,780 --> 00:18:40,500
What? You can't be serious?!

387
00:18:40,560 --> 00:18:42,470
I'm trying out
the Colonel's sport.

388
00:18:42,620 --> 00:18:44,310
Think I might be able to catch a few fish.

389
00:18:50,680 --> 00:18:54,020
We're using brother as bait
to lure out the Homunculi

390
00:18:54,080 --> 00:18:55,430
He's too important to them.

391
00:18:55,680 --> 00:18:57,800
They can't afford to just let him die.

392
00:18:58,240 --> 00:18:59,420
That's crazy!

393
00:18:59,480 --> 00:19:01,640
We're not gonna let
anyone else get hurt.

394
00:19:01,790 --> 00:19:04,740
Using ourselves as bait
was our only option.

395
00:19:05,820 --> 00:19:08,340
What are you going to do
if Scar happens to get shot?

396
00:19:08,500 --> 00:19:10,880
The MPs might get here before the Homunculi.

397
00:19:10,920 --> 00:19:13,700
But you can stop that from happening.
Can't you, Colonel?

398
00:19:14,150 --> 00:19:16,190
So now I take orders
from you, is that it?

399
00:19:16,540 --> 00:19:18,060
You've got a lot of nerve.

400
00:19:19,020 --> 00:19:21,180
You had better plan on
sharing what you catch.

401
00:19:21,180 --> 00:19:22,240
Of course!

402
00:19:43,480 --> 00:19:46,060
Hey, get out of the way!
We need a clear shot.

403
00:19:46,060 --> 00:19:48,520
Don't shoot! You'll hit my brother!

404
00:19:48,940 --> 00:19:50,160
Dammit!

405
00:19:50,160 --> 00:19:52,580
Everything's lost if
those guys shoot Scar.

406
00:19:52,740 --> 00:19:54,320
How long can I keep this up?

407
00:19:54,500 --> 00:19:55,760
Way too close!

408
00:19:55,760 --> 00:19:57,760
Hurry up, you stupid Homunculi!

409
00:19:58,840 --> 00:20:01,380
Which channel's
the Provost Marshal's?

410
00:20:01,550 --> 00:20:02,030
Got it.

411
00:20:02,570 --> 00:20:04,650
You haven't let me down, Fuery..

412
00:20:06,020 --> 00:20:08,600
Attention, this is Sector 3 patrol.

413
00:20:08,600 --> 00:20:11,640
We're under attack from Scar,
request immediate backup—

414
00:20:11,800 --> 00:20:15,040
What? No! No—[SCREAMS]

415
00:20:15,040 --> 00:20:17,100
All right, onto Sector 17.

416
00:20:17,100 --> 00:20:19,200
[GIGGLING]
This is pretty fun!

417
00:20:19,420 --> 00:20:20,700
[LOW VOICE] Come in!
[DIFFERENT VOICE] Come in!

418
00:20:21,500 --> 00:20:22,860
But that can't be right...

419
00:20:22,960 --> 00:20:25,530
He's in Sector 17?
What about Sector 3?!

420
00:20:25,880 --> 00:20:26,920
Colonel Douglas!

421
00:20:27,100 --> 00:20:29,200
He's in Sector 8, now!
What's that?!

422
00:20:30,180 --> 00:20:32,380
MP HQ calling Sector 8.

423
00:20:32,680 --> 00:20:34,810
Scar is currently
fighting a young man.

424
00:20:34,930 --> 00:20:36,850
The young man is
a State Alchemist.

425
00:20:37,090 --> 00:20:38,330
Do not fire!

426
00:20:38,780 --> 00:20:40,260
Multiple reports in all sectors!

427
00:20:40,270 --> 00:20:41,840
We have reports of a fourth Scar!

428
00:20:41,920 --> 00:20:44,100
This is Sector 3,
all streets are clear.

429
00:20:44,300 --> 00:20:47,860
Sector 8 requesting backup!
Currently engaged with Scar!

430
00:20:53,040 --> 00:20:54,560
Come now, Gluttony.

431
00:20:54,560 --> 00:20:56,360
I smell the Ishvalan.

432
00:20:56,440 --> 00:20:58,360
He's here,
I get to eat him, right?!

433
00:21:00,280 --> 00:21:01,880
That's a strange presence.

434
00:21:01,880 --> 00:21:03,560
You could feel it too, right?

435
00:21:03,560 --> 00:21:04,660
Yes.

436
00:21:04,660 --> 00:21:06,140
Then it's time to move.

437
00:21:09,800 --> 00:21:11,220
Which will it be?

438
00:21:11,240 --> 00:21:13,540
Is he gonna destroy
my body or my automail?

439
00:21:13,540 --> 00:21:14,620
Brother!

440
00:21:21,720 --> 00:21:22,960
Lucky!

441
00:21:24,010 --> 00:21:26,270
He cancelled out Scar's alchemy!

442
00:21:26,470 --> 00:21:28,330
How reckless can you get?!

443
00:21:29,520 --> 00:21:31,430
He's got tattoo!

444
00:21:31,980 --> 00:21:33,080
Bastard!

445
00:21:33,610 --> 00:21:35,240
You were the one!

446
00:21:35,400 --> 00:21:38,140
I smell him!
Time to eat!

447
00:21:43,820 --> 00:21:45,800
Hi! How's it going?

448
00:21:46,180 --> 00:21:48,490
That is one pretty unusual
body you've got there.

449
00:21:49,210 --> 00:21:51,740
Just how many people
are inside you?

450
00:21:52,240 --> 00:21:53,810
Oh, you!

451
00:21:54,070 --> 00:21:55,700
Don't bother running.

452
00:21:55,870 --> 00:21:57,490
I sense your presence.

453
00:21:57,820 --> 00:21:59,420
And I can follow it.

454
00:21:59,840 --> 00:22:00,680
Follow? Me?

455
00:22:00,790 --> 00:22:01,790
Me?

456
00:22:02,660 --> 00:22:05,280
Then I'll just eat you now!

457
00:22:05,680 --> 00:22:06,310
There it is!

458
00:22:06,440 --> 00:22:07,960
He's a Homunculus!

459
00:22:08,410 --> 00:22:08,920
So,

460
00:22:09,350 --> 00:22:12,020
you're able to detect
his presence, are you?

461
00:22:14,620 --> 00:22:16,730
Well that's quite the nuisance.

462
00:22:17,540 --> 00:22:18,920
Let's take care of it.

463
00:22:20,800 --> 00:22:22,460
Lan Fan! Run!

464
00:22:25,640 --> 00:22:27,200
No! Lan Fan!

465
00:22:28,860 --> 00:22:34,400
Let it all out, let it all out

466
00:22:34,400 --> 00:22:38,760
Tsuyogaranakute ii n da ne

467
00:22:39,760 --> 00:22:45,100
Dareka ga kaite'tta

468
00:22:45,100 --> 00:22:51,120
Kabe no rakugaki no hana ga yureru

469
00:22:51,580 --> 00:22:56,820
Jibunrashisa nante, dare mo wakaranai yo

470
00:22:56,820 --> 00:23:02,200
Nagai nagai michi no tochuu
de nakushitari, hirottari, 

471
00:23:02,720 --> 00:23:11,960
Kyuu ni samishiku natte,
naichau hi mo aru kedo

472
00:23:12,160 --> 00:23:17,580
Namida mo itami mo, hoshi ni kaeyou

473
00:23:17,660 --> 00:23:23,840
Ashita wo terasu akari wo tomosou

474
00:23:23,840 --> 00:23:31,780
Chiisana te kazashite
futari de tsukurou hoshikuzu wo

475
00:23:31,780 --> 00:23:34,040
Tsuyoku hikaru ein wo

476
00:23:34,040 --> 00:23:39,340
Sayonara itsuka wa kuru ka mo shirenu

477
00:23:39,340 --> 00:23:45,560
Kisetsu wa sore demo meguri megutte'ku

478
00:23:45,560 --> 00:23:53,200
Chiisaku mayotte mo aruite'ku
Kimi to aruite'ku

479
00:23:53,440 --> 00:23:57,740
Sore daku wa kawaranaide iyou ne

480
00:24:00,140 --> 00:24:04,280
The scream of the fallen girl pierces
every darkened corner of Central.

481
00:24:04,960 --> 00:24:08,620
As the anguished debts of a violent history
are repaid with bloodshed,

482
00:24:08,720 --> 00:24:13,180
the past and present reveal themselves
to be murderous reflections of one another.

483
00:24:14,120 --> 00:24:16,790
Next time on Fullmetal Alchemist: Brotherhood

484
00:24:17,500 --> 00:24:21,480
Episode 22: Backs in the Distance

485
00:24:22,100 --> 00:24:26,840
The young man realized... He'd do anything to protect her.
